% // Three thousand years in one column. Nobody wrote this page: it is every
% // dated event from every rewritten article, sorted, banded and linked back
% // to the article it came from.
< section class="index-head"
  <p class="eyebrow">{{ req.count }} dated events · {{ req.articles }} articles · one column
  <h1>Timeline
  <p>Every date the corpus knows, in order. Each one belongs to an article and links back to it; nothing here was written for this page. Where a source dates something to a millennium, it sits in the middle of that millennium, because that is the only honest place to put it.

< div class="timeline"
  % for (const band of req.bands) {
  < section class="band"
    <h2 id="{{ band.key }}">{{ band.label }}
    < div class="band-events"
      % for (const event of band.events) {
      < div class="event"
        <p class="event-when">{{ event.when }}
        < div class="event-what"
          {{ event.what }}
          <p class="event-from">[[ {{ event.title }} | {{ event.url }} ]]
      % }
  % }
